282	/**
283	 * The late charge as of the sheet's today: an OPEN (or PENDING) claim past its due-by (fixed when it was added) gains the late
284	 * percent in force on its date of its figure for every full 30 days it is overdue, rounded to two decimals as the claim rounds (see
285	 * {@link #rounding}). A correction
286	 * (a negative amount) never gains one. The charge is never bound by a statement; settling freezes it into the settled due.
287	 */
288	    /**
289	     * How the claim's live figures round: half up when it is dated before the policy date, half to even on or after
290	     * it. A correction rounds by the date of the claim it corrects.
291	     */
